<title>GERMANY: Karstadt sees 1996 earnings lagging.</title>
<headline>Karstadt sees 1996 earnings lagging.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German retail group Karstadt AG said on Friday that it expected its full-year earnings to be below those achieved last year.</p>
<p>In a mandatory statement, Karstadt said its sales development in the third quarter had been disappointing but operating earnings had gone according to plan.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a slight pick-up in business at the start of the fourth quarter, but its continuation in the Christmas season will not be enough to balance out the earnings lag against the previous year,&quot; the group said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
